    <briefdescription>
<para>Propagates assumption information from parent functions to all of their successors. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>An assumption can be propagated if the containing function dominates the called function.</para>
<para>We start with a &quot;known&quot; set of assumptions already valid for the associated function and an &quot;assumed&quot; set that initially contains all possible assumptions. The assumed set is inter-procedurally updated by narrowing its contents as concrete values are known. The concrete values are seeded by the first nodes that are either entries into the call graph, or contains no assumptions. Each node is updated as the intersection of the assumed state with all of its predecessors. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
